<article class="env-definition" id="023V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/023V">Definition <span data-tag="023V">35.34.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $V \to X$ be a scheme over $X$. A <em>descent datum for $V/X/S$</em> is an isomorphism $\varphi : V \times _ S X \to X \times _ S V$ of schemes over $X \times _ S X$ satisfying the <em>cocycle condition</em> that the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ V \times _ S X \times _ S X \ar[rd]^{\varphi _{01}} \ar[rr]_{\varphi _{02}} &  &  X \times _ S X \times _ S V\\  &  X \times _ S V \times _ S X \ar[ru]^{\varphi _{12}} }  \]
</div>
<p>
 commutes (with obvious notation). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We also say that the pair $(V/X, \varphi )$ is a <em>descent datum relative to $X \to S$</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism $g : (V/X, \varphi ) \to (V'/X, \varphi ')$ of descent data relative to $X \to S$</em> is a morphism $g : V \to V'$ of schemes over $X$ such that the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ V \times _ S X \ar[r]_{\varphi } \ar[d]_{g \times \text{id}_ X} &  X \times _ S V \ar[d]^{\text{id}_ X \times g} \\  V' \times _ S X \ar[r]^{\varphi '} &  X \times _ S V' }  \]
</div>
<p>
 commutes. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>